{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the main results of Dubova, Yang, Yau and Yin, \"Delocalization of non-mean-field random matrices in dimensions d >= 3\" (arXiv:2507.20274). The model is the Gaussian block band matrix on the torus Z_{WL}^d with L^d blocks of size W^d, N = (WL)^d, with the variance profile (2.5) under the size conditions (2.9), (2.10). For every dimension d >= 3, this entry contains Theorem 2.1 (delocalization of the bulk eigenvectors), Theorem 2.2 (the local law, (2.14)-(2.15)), Theorem 2.3 (quantum unique ergodicity, (2.18)-(2.19)) and Theorem 2.5 (quantum diffusion, (2.22)-(2.25)); they have no hypotheses other than their parameters, and no result of another work is assumed for them. The library also proves Theorem 2.4 (bulk universality) and Theorem 2.7 (the block Anderson model) from one external input, stated as an explicit hypothesis; those two are not part of this entry.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jun Yin"
